1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
[SCREAMING]

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,750
…and that's my front door this Halloween.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,695
This is an AI Halloween system.

4
00:00:09,745 --> 00:00:13,633
It watches your driveway, figures out if
a kid or an adult is coming, and gives

5
00:00:13,683 --> 00:00:17,871
each of them the right show: cute and silly
for kids, properly terrifying for adults.

6
00:00:17,921 --> 00:00:20,812
And you can have it running at
your house in under an hour.

7
00:00:20,862 --> 00:00:22,656
No coding, no cloud, no subscription.

8
00:00:22,706 --> 00:00:24,750
You just download it, copy it, and run it.

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,332
Here's everything you need: any
computer running Windows or Linux.

10
00:00:30,382 --> 00:00:32,452
Mine's a cheap old Celeron.

11
00:00:32,502 --> 00:00:35,514
A monitor or TV, the bigger the better.

12
00:00:35,564 --> 00:00:39,283
Any USB webcam; I'm using
a basic Logitech C270.

13
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:40,303
And speakers.

14
00:00:40,353 --> 00:00:41,088
That's it.

15
00:00:41,138 --> 00:00:44,622
It's a 154 MB download,
takes about 300 MB on

16
00:00:44,672 --> 00:00:48,233
disk, and uses one to
two gigabytes of memory.

17
00:00:48,283 --> 00:00:54,750
After the download it runs completely
offline, and nothing is recorded or uploaded.

18
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,479
Here's the plan.

19
00:00:56,529 --> 00:00:59,386
Five minutes to download and unzip.

20
00:00:59,436 --> 00:01:01,711
Fifteen to place the camera.

21
00:01:01,761 --> 00:01:08,189
Fifteen to draw the zones and teach it
the difference between kids and adults.

22
00:01:08,239 --> 00:01:09,186
Ten to test.

23
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:14,750
And it gets its voices ready by
itself while you put out the candy.

24
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,168
Go to the GitHub link in the description,

25
00:01:18,218 --> 00:01:21,481
click Releases, and
download the Windows zip.

26
00:01:21,531 --> 00:01:25,677
Unzip it somewhere permanent,
like C:\SpookyTreatStation.

27
00:01:25,727 --> 00:01:27,812
Then double-click Setup Mode.

28
00:01:27,862 --> 00:01:32,082
Windows will warn you because
it's not from a big company.

29
00:01:32,132 --> 00:01:34,511
Click More info, then Run anyway.

30
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:38,560
It's free and open source,
so anyone can read the code.

31
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,548
On Linux it's just as easy.

32
00:01:40,598 --> 00:01:43,051
Unpack it and run install.sh once.

33
00:01:43,101 --> 00:01:46,437
If you don't have Chrome,
it offers to install

34
00:01:46,487 --> 00:01:49,750
it for you, then puts
the icons in your menu.

35
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:53,547
This is the one thing that matters.

36
00:01:53,597 --> 00:01:59,176
The AI needs to see people
head to toe while they walk up.

37
00:01:59,226 --> 00:02:05,971
My first try was tilting the camera
way down, and all it saw was legs.

38
00:02:06,021 --> 00:02:12,474
❌ The fix: put the camera about
two metres high, a couple of metres

39
00:02:12,524 --> 00:02:19,171
behind the screen, tilted just
slightly down, looking along the path.

40
00:02:19,221 --> 00:02:24,800
If it sits on top of the
monitor, tilt it only a tiny bit.

41
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:27,809
Add a porch light if it's dark.

42
00:02:27,859 --> 00:02:29,750
The AI likes to see.

43
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,867
In setup you see what the AI sees, live.

44
00:02:33,917 --> 00:02:38,791
Drag the yellow line to
where visitors start counting

45
00:02:38,841 --> 00:02:44,459
(everything past it, like the
street, is ignored), the orange

46
00:02:44,509 --> 00:02:51,335
line just before the candy, and the
red line right in front of the screen.

47
00:02:51,385 --> 00:02:55,145
Then have an adult stand far away, in the

48
00:02:55,195 --> 00:02:59,512
middle and up close, and
hit Capture each time.

49
00:02:59,562 --> 00:03:03,414
Now it knows how tall people look at every

50
00:03:03,464 --> 00:03:08,618
distance, so it can tell a
five-year-old from their dad.

51
00:03:08,668 --> 00:03:13,728
Press Save, then Close, and
the show starts right away.

52
00:03:13,778 --> 00:03:14,750
No restart.

53
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:21,197
Walk up your driveway and watch it go.

54
00:03:21,247 --> 00:03:27,881
When nobody's there, it invites people in.

55
00:03:27,931 --> 00:03:34,247
When someone steps in, it welcomes them.

56
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:41,090
At the candy, it tells
you: one per person.

57
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:44,591
And when you reach in…

58
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,701
The characters talk with natural AI voices

59
00:03:48,751 --> 00:03:52,505
generated right on your
PC, not in the cloud.

60
00:03:52,555 --> 00:03:58,169
The first time, it prepares every
sentence in the background, which

61
00:03:58,219 --> 00:04:04,171
takes a few minutes on a slow PC, so
do it while you set out the candy.

62
00:04:04,221 --> 00:04:05,777
Don't like a voice?

63
00:04:05,827 --> 00:04:07,298
Hit Another voice.

64
00:04:07,348 --> 00:04:09,750
There are 904 to choose from.

65
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:40,000
[REACTIONS AND LAUGHTER]

66
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:45,322
That's it: an AI scare system
in under an hour, for free.

67
00:04:45,372 --> 00:04:48,952
The download link is in the description.

68
00:04:49,002 --> 00:04:53,580
Build one, film the reactions,
and send them to me.

69
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:57,209
The best ones go in the follow-up video.

70
00:04:57,259 --> 00:04:58,661
Happy Halloween…

71
00:04:58,711 --> 00:04:59,750
if you dare.

